OL,3,GNorth East
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FA dry and bright day with a mix
OL,6,Fof sunny spells and the odd coastal
OL,7,Fshower possible, but these clearing to
OL,8,Fthe south during the afternoon. After
OL,9,Fa cool start, temperatures climbing to
OL,10,Faround average in the sunshine.
OL,11,
OL,12,CTonight:FA bright end to the day with
OL,13,Fsunny spells this evening. Remaining
OL,14,Fdry overnight with clear spells
OL,15,Fdeveloping. Rather chilly,
OL,16,Fparticularly in rural spots.
OL,17,
OL,18,CSunday:FDry and settled for most on
OL,19,FSunday, with plenty of late August
OL,20,Fsunshine on offer. Light winds and
OL,21,Ffeeling warm in the sunshine.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
